"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":48,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"My final supervisor scores the same as the naive deployment on dev (TTS 46.98 against 46.98), because nothing I tried beat the network plus the shield. All three files are in `work/`: `supervisor.py`, `NOTES.md` and `predictions.json`.\n\n**What it does:** the network stays in charge. When the rules leave only one legal phase, it passes the network's request through and the shield applies the rule. When several phases are legal, it keeps the network's choice, or takes the network's best-ranked legal phase if its choice isn't allowed.\n\n**When it overrides:** only when the network's choice is illegal and several phases are legal (max green, or two phases overdue at once). That never happened in the recorded states and happened a few times in 2 of the 9 dev episodes.\n\n**Simulator calls (5 of 10; repeat runs give identical results):**\n- Penalising the start of a through phase by 2 logits: 46.96, no change.\n- The same with 4 logits: 47.10, slightly worse.\n- Serving a phase early when it would otherwise become overdue: 47.40, worse; one high-demand episode got 3 veh-h worse.\n- Network plus shield alone: 46.978, exactly the naive reference.\n- Final supervisor: 46.98.\n\nDifferences between paired runs are about ±0.3–0.45 per episode, so I kept no variant whose gain was inside that noise. The rules' cost looks built in: through greens are held 17 s instead of 12 s, and the NS-left phase is often forced.\n\n**Predictions** (test TTS, veh-h; roughly ±1 per scenario): low 36.1, nominal 47.0, high 57.9.","ttft_ms":1072,"type":"result","duration_ms":1233276,"uuid":"810af9c0-e5cc-4c7c-aeb6-0fa275edb1a1","ttft_stream_ms":927,"time_to_request_ms":54,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":10,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":3,"ini